title: Relation traversal in queries and result rows (+@cascade semantics)
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-10T05:18:42'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T09:45:17'
result: Implemented belongs-to relation traversal. `&owner as Owner` is now a real
  stored I64 sid column (previously dropped entirely from the schema). Traversing
  `row.owner` resolves the stored sid against the target store's primary (sid) index
  and yields a `Row Owner` whose fields read directly (`row.owner.name`). Relation
  columns are insertable and queryable (`count pets where owner eq 2`). Has-many (`&items
  as [Item]`) is rejected with a precise diagnostic steering to an explicit `all Item
  where <fk> eq Store.sid` query rather than guessing the foreign key. `@cascade`
  parses and compiles as a documented no-op (real cascade delete deferred — no runtime
  infra and ambiguous FK resolution). New conformance suite tests/store_relations.rs
  (4 tests) pins all semantics; full test suite green (zero regressions, zero warnings).
description: 'Item 4. &owner as Owner / &items as [Item] become queryable: o.customer
  resolves foreign sid via target store primary index; has-many yields typed row sets;
  @cascade gains real delete/destroy semantics. Or remove relation syntax if infeasible.
  Tests for traversal + cascade.'
